  "statement": "While I recognize the importance of energy efficiency (GRN-01) and the need for emergency protocols (GRN-07), I emphasize that security cannot be compromised. The conflicts raised regarding GRN-07's potential impact on secure remote updates (TRU-06) are concerning. I propose to modify GRN-07 to ensure that energy reduction during critical failures does not impede the secure functioning of the system. Additionally, I support the need to maintain data integrity (TRU-01) while ensuring timely responses during emergencies, thus proposing a synthesis that ensures both security and emergency responsiveness.",
